[=#mysqlauth]
= Authentication/Encryption Options =

When using the !MySQL protocol, there are several options for controlling which users are allowed to access an instance of SQL Relay.

* [mysqlprotoconnectstringsauth.html Connect Strings Auth]
* [mysqlprotouserlistauth.html User List Auth]
* [mysqlprotodbauth.html Database Auth]
* [mysqlprototls.html TLS/SSL Encryption and Authentication]

